      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "i'll Pretty much reflect what i said on Reddit.\n\nthis can be both a boon to RP'ers and those w/ D.I.D alike. I could see this also being abused by people initially trying to impersonate leading atleast an need for either client sided options to enforce default account names or, Instance host options to Disable \"Character Name plates.\" or in the case of a group+ instance, lock to group members only.   (that'd allow control for RP Sessions/groups to prevent impersonators.)\n\ni've seen other platforms gracefully handle this to the degree of Client side can toggle between turning names off entirely to enforcing defaults only or allowing Customs. \n\nit'd be widespread adopted if it was made available to both Normal users as well as VRC+ members alike, sadly? the path they've been taking towards customization especially when it comes to something cosmetic like this? .. it wont.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
